From 83610f6847e34d81c1e79c4870e812e95d6d6a2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takumi Ando <takumi@spacecubics.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:48:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] spi: zynqmp-gqspi: Select independent upper chip select

The GQSPI driver only selects the upper chip select when SPI NOR marks
an operation as accessing the upper half of a stacked memory. An
independent device with reg = <1> therefore accesses the lower chip
select instead.

Use the physical chip select for independent devices while retaining
the existing stacked-memory flag handling.

Signed-off-by: Takumi Ando <takumi@spacecubics.com>
---
 drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c b/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c
index 4251bf28cd3..c446ac15610 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/zynqmp_gqspi.c
@@ -857,7 +857,8 @@ static int zynqmp_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
 	priv->rx_buf = op->data.buf.in;
 	priv->len = op->data.nbytes;
 
-	if (slave->flags & SPI_XFER_U_PAGE)
+	if ((slave->flags & SPI_XFER_U_PAGE) ||
+	    spi_chip_select(slave->dev) == 1)
 		priv->u_page = 1;
 	else
 		priv->u_page = 0;
